<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>What types of revenue should be excluded from MRR?</h3>
    <p>Exclude one-off setup fees, custom implementation services, hardware sales, and non-recurring professional consulting revenue. MRR measures strictly predictable subscription cash flows.</p>

    <h3>How do annual upfront payments affect MRR calculations?</h3>
    <p>If a customer pays $1,200 upfront for an annual subscription, divide the total payment by 12 months to record $100 per month in MRR rather than recording $1,200 in a single month.</p>

    <h3>What is Net New MRR?</h3>
    <p>Net New MRR equals New MRR plus Expansion MRR minus Contraction MRR and Churned MRR. Net New MRR measures overall monthly revenue momentum.</p>
</section>

